    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Type of Offence",
          "Composition Amount*"
        ],
        [
          "Leaving Singapore in a Singapore registered motor vehicle with less than three-quarter tank full of motor fuel",
          "Motor Vehicles (Sedan, SUV, MPV, Hatchback, Convertible, etc.)\n1st offence: S$100\n2nd offence: S$300\n3rd offence: S$500\nLarge-Sized Motor Vehicles (Goods Vehicles, Trucks, Buses, Vans,\netc.)\n1st offence: S$300\n2nd offence: S$400\n3rd offence: S$500"
        ]
      ],
      "hyperlinks": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The driver may be required to turn back to Singapore to refill the fuel tank to three-quarters full before leaving. The driver may be charged in court if the fuel gauge has been tampered with.",
      "formatting": {
        "bold_ratio": 0.0,
        "mostly_bold": false,
        "max_font_size_pt": null
      },
      "list": {
        "is_list_item": false,
        "level": null,
        "num_id": null,
        "detected_from": null
      },
      "hyperlinks": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Common reasons such as being unaware of the rule, forgetting to refuel, or experiencing traffic delays are generally not considered sufficient grounds for an appeal.",
      "formatting": {
        "bold_ratio": 0.0,
        "mostly_bold": false,
        "max_font_size_pt": null
      },
      "list": {
        "is_list_item": false,
        "level": null,
        "num_id": null,
        "detected_from": null
      },
      "hyperlinks": []
    },
